            <ArticleTitle>Papilloedema secondary to acute purulent sinusitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>396-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Upper respiratory tract infections and sinusitis are common, but intracranial complications of sinusitis are rare in children and are often clinically unremarkable. Papilloedema secondary to purulent sinusitis is a complication previously not reported. We report two cases to highlight atypical manifestations of sinusitis in children.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
